━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  FREE:   Run Meridian locally or self-host internally for any purpose —
          personal, commercial, research, internal tooling. Any team size.
          Connecting to a hosted database (Neon, Supabase, etc.) is free.
          Writing internal deployment guides for your own organization is free.

  PAID:   Hosting Meridian as a service for others. Building a competing
          coordination platform for third parties. Publishing open-internet
          guides or tooling whose primary purpose is enabling third parties
          to commercially operate Meridian or a Competing Use product.

  NEVER:  The above during the Protection Period without a commercial
          license from us.

  LATER:  After 5 years from first public release of each version, that
          version automatically becomes MIT — no strings attached.

