1. DEFINITIONS

   "Licensor" means Adam Camerer, copyright holder of the Software.

   "Software" means the Meridian source code, binaries, documentation,
   and all associated files distributed under this license.

   "Protection Period" means five (5) years from the date each version
   of the Software is first publicly distributed. Each version carries
   its own independent Protection Period from its own release date.

   "Change Date" means the date five (5) years after the first public
   distribution date of a given version of the Software.

   "Change License" means the MIT License
   (https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT).

   "Competing Use" means making the Software or a functionally similar
   product available to third parties as a hosted or managed service —
   specifically, providing shared goal state, session coordination, task
   queuing, or human-in-the-loop workflow functionality to users outside
   your own organization. Internal use within your own organization,
   regardless of organization size, is not Competing Use.

   "Commercial Deployment Guide" means any publicly accessible
   documentation, tutorial, blog post, video, Helm chart, Docker Compose
   file, or similar material whose primary purpose is enabling third
   parties to operate the Software commercially or as a multi-tenant
   service. Internal deployment documentation for your own organization's
   use, and general tutorials about using Meridian as a user, are
   explicitly not Commercial Deployment Guides.

   "Local Use" means installation and operation of the Software on
   machines owned or controlled by you or your organization, where
   access is limited to members of your own organization.

2. GRANT OF RIGHTS

   Subject to the terms and conditions of this License, and except for
   Competing Use as defined above, the Licensor grants you a worldwide,
   royalty-free, non-sublicensable, non-exclusive license to:

   a) Use, copy, modify, and distribute the Software for any purpose,
      including commercial purposes within your own organization.

   b) Self-host the Software internally for any team size, connecting
      to external hosted databases as needed.

   c) Run the Software in CI/CD pipelines and automated workflows for
      your own projects.

   d) Use the Software for academic, research, and educational purposes,
      including publication of findings.

   e) Write internal deployment documentation, scripts, and tooling for
      your own organization's use.

   f) Distribute unmodified copies for evaluation or non-commercial
      purposes, provided this license is retained in full.

3. RESTRICTIONS

   During the Protection Period, the following are not permitted without
   a separate written commercial license from the Licensor:

   a) Competing Use — making the Software or a functionally similar
      product available to third parties as a hosted or managed service.

   b) Publishing Commercial Deployment Guides — openly distributing
      guides, tooling, or materials whose primary purpose is enabling
      third parties to commercially operate the Software.

   c) White-labeling — distributing the Software or derivatives with
      Licensor attribution removed or obscured, for the purpose of
      offering it as a competing product or service.

   d) AI Training Use — using the Software, its source code, or
      documentation as training data for machine learning models
      intended for commercial distribution or sale without prior
      written permission from the Licensor.

   e) Sublicensing or reselling the Software or derivatives as a
      standalone commercial product for third parties.

4. PATENT GRANT

   Subject to the terms of this License, the Licensor hereby grants
   you a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive patent
   license to make, use, sell, and distribute the Software, solely
   to the extent necessary to exercise the rights granted in Section 2.
   This patent grant does not extend to Competing Use or any use
   restricted under Section 3.

5. LICENSE CONVERSION

